      "message": "You\u0027ll probably wonder why bother with a `Context` struct wrapper around `Options`, given that there\u0027s only the one member. Two reasons:\n1. We do this for the wgsl fuzzer, where we actually did add another member. We may add more members in the future, and modifying this one struct is way easier than modifying the multiple places that deal with this arg.\n2. Adding an argument named \"Options\" is super confusing when the fuzzer function also has an argument named \"Options\" for backend options.",
